```lean
import DoCarmoLib
import UpstreamAdapters.Adapters

/-!
# Pointwise curvature-form symmetries with minimal hypotheses (U1 consumers)

The upstream development states the symmetries of the metric-lowered curvature
`(0,4)`-form in two places:

* field level, for *any* connection (`AffineConnection.curvatureForm_antisymm_left`),
  for a metric-compatible connection (`…_antisymm_right`), for a symmetric
  connection (`…_bianchi`), and for a symmetric metric-compatible connection
  (`…_pairSwap`);
* pointwise, but only bundled for the **Levi-Civita** connection inside
  `AffineConnection.isAlgCurvatureForm_curvatureFormAt` (which requires
  `nabla.IsLeviCivita g` and installs a local `RiemannianBundle` instance).

This module exposes the four symmetries as named *pointwise* lemmas with the
hypotheses each one actually needs.  They are derived consumers — each proof
rewrites the pointwise form to the field-level form with the upstream
`curvatureFormAt_eq` tensoriality bridge and applies the upstream field lemma —
not new mathematics.  The genuinely new pointwise **operator** statements are in
`UpstreamAdapters.DownstreamGeometry`.
-/
```

Then the lemmas. Context variables: copy from DownstreamGeometry's General section, but note `curvatureForm_antisymm_right` etc. require `[CompleteSpace E]`, `[I.Boundaryless]` for some. Let me match a variable block that satisfies all:

```lean
section General
variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E]
variable {H : Type*} [TopologicalSpace H] {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} [I.Boundaryless]
variable {M : Type*} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M] [IsManifold I ∞ M]
```

Note probe showed `[inst_6 : IsManifold I (↑⊤) M]` — i.e., `IsManifold I ∞ M` in Lean 4.32 (∞ = ⊤?). In DownstreamGeometry they used `[IsManifold I ∞ M]`. OK.

Lemma 1:
```lean
theorem curvatureFormAt_skew_fst (nabla : AffineConnection I M) (g : RiemannianMetric I M)
    (p : M) (x y z t : TangentSpace I p) :
    nabla.curvatureFormAt g p x y z t = -nabla.curvatureFormAt g p y x z t := by
  rw [nabla.curvatureFormAt_eq g p (AffineConnection.extendField_apply p x)
      (AffineConnection.extendField_apply p y) (AffineConnection.extendField_apply p z)
      (AffineConnection.extendField_apply p t),
    nabla.curvatureFormAt_eq g p (AffineConnection.extendField_apply p y)
      (AffineConnection.extendField_apply p x) (AffineConnection.extendField_apply p z)
      (AffineConnection.extendField_apply p t)]
  exact nabla.curvatureForm_antisymm_left g _ _ _ _ p
```

Careful: `curvatureFormAt_eq` signature from the source: 
`theorem curvatureFormAt_eq (g : RiemannianMetric I M) (p : M) {x y z t : TangentSpace I p} {X Y Z T : SmoothVectorField I M} (hX : X p = x) (hY : Y p = y) (hZ : Z p = z) (hT : T p = t) : nabla.curvatureFormAt g p x y z t = nabla.curvatureForm g X Y Z T p`

In DownstreamGeometry they wrote `rw [AffineConnection.curvatureOperatorAt_eq (nabla := ...) p (extendField_apply p u) ...]` — for curvatureFormAt_eq: `nabla.curvatureFormAt_eq g p (extendField_apply p x) ...`. The implicit x y z t are inferred from the goal. Should work.

Lemma 2:
```lean
theorem curvatureFormAt_skew_snd_of_isMetricCompatible (nabla : AffineConnection I M)
    (g : RiemannianMetric I M) (hcompat : nabla.IsMetricCompatible g) (p : M)
    (x y z t : TangentSpace I p) :
    nabla.curvatureFormAt g p x y z t = -nabla.curvatureFormAt g p x y t z := by
  rw [...two rewrites with z,t swapped...]
  exact nabla.curvatureForm_antisymm_right g hcompat _ _ _ _ p
```
Check `IsMetricCompatible` argument order: probe says `AffineConnection.IsMetricCompatible g nabla` (g first). But in the file `curvatureForm_antisymm_right (hcompat : nabla.IsMetricCompatible g)` — dot notation `nabla.IsMetricCompatible g` = `IsMetricCompatible g nabla`. So as a hypothesis I write `(hcompat : nabla.IsMetricCompatible g)`. Good.

Lemma 3:
```lean
theorem curvatureFormAt_bianchi_of_isSymmetric (nabla : AffineConnection I M)
    (g : RiemannianMetric I M) (hsym : nabla.IsSymmetric) (p : M) (x y z t : TangentSpace I p) :
    nabla.curvatureFormAt g p x y z t + nabla.curvatureFormAt g p y z x t
      + nabla.curvatureFormAt g p z x y t = 0 := by
  rw [three rewrites]
  exact nabla.curvatureForm_bianchi g hsym _ _ _ _ p
```
Note: `curvatureForm_bianchi` signature probe: `(nabla) (g) : nabla.IsSymmetric → ∀ X Y Z T p, ...` so `nabla.curvatureForm_bianchi g hsym X Y Z T p`. In DoCarmoCh4 they write `nabla.curvatureForm_bianchi g hsym Y Z X T p`. Good.

Lemma 4:
```lean
theorem curvatureFormAt_pairSwap_of_isSymmetric_of_isMetricCompatible
    (nabla : AffineConnection I M) (g : RiemannianMetric I M) (hsym : nabla.IsSymmetric)
    (hcompat : nabla.IsMetricCompatible g) (p : M) (x y z t : TangentSpace I p) :
    nabla.curvatureFormAt g p x y z t = nabla.curvatureFormAt g p z t x y := by
  rw [two rewrites]
  exact nabla.curvatureForm_pairSwap g hsym hcompat _ _ _ _ p
```

